_notice() {
  cat <<'EOF'

kbrgb: the udev rule is installed. If the keyboard still needs sudo,
replug it or reboot once so the rule is applied.

The five reactive effects (typewriter, keyflash, wpmheat, zen, flow) read
key events from /dev/input, which needs your user in the input group:

    sudo usermod -aG input $USER      # then log out and back in

Every other effect works without it. Keycodes are used in memory only,
never stored, logged or sent anywhere.

EOF
}

post_install() {
  udevadm control --reload-rules >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  udevadm trigger >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  _notice
}

post_upgrade() {
  udevadm control --reload-rules >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  udevadm trigger >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}
